Package: claw-os-systemd
Version: __VERSION__
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Claw OS <noreply@github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/xiaoyu-work/claw-os
Depends: claw-os-base (= __VERSION__), systemd, systemd-coredump,
 init-system-helpers (>= 1.52)
Description: Claw OS — systemd integration for Claw OS targets
 Installs systemd units for booting and running Claw OS on Docker, WSL,
 ISO, and VM targets. Specifically:
 .
   * cos-home-setup.service — sets up the agent-home OverlayFS at
     boot (target path from /etc/default/cos-home; enabled by default).
   * cos-browser.service — runs the cos-browser CDP server on port
     9222 (installed but not enabled; opt-in).
   * clawd.service — starts the boot-time system agent daemon.
   * systemd-coredump — captures process crashes for Crash Doctor.
   * claw-recoll-index.service and claw-semantic.service — maintain
     per-user keyword and semantic indexes under graphical or headless
     user sessions (enabled globally; skipped when optional binaries
     are absent).
 .
 Docker, WSL, ISO, and VM images all use these units so clawd is started
 by the same system boot path everywhere.
